<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  datamodel="sce-static" (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15): one copy of a shared
  to-do list, for the world simulation (backends/rust/world). Every copy is the same
  document, and no copy is special.

  A to-do is a row of fields: a title, whether it is done, a due day, whether it is
  removed, and the fields of its schedule. The numbers of the fields are the host's. Each
  field of each to-do is a multi-value register: a write gives the field one more value,
  known by the stamp of the write (its dot), and a person who writes over a field writes
  over the values they have SEEN, no others. So two people who change the same field of
  one to-do at once, neither having seen the other's write, both keep theirs, on every
  copy, whatever order the changes reach it in; and a person who writes after seeing
  them replaces them all. A field with one value reads as that value, and with more than
  one says it was changed twice at once, and which values, for a person to choose from.

  The list's protocol is the standard shared record list's (sce:std/shared/record_list,
  docs/adr/0042, docs/adr/0085): a change is one message, `record_list.change`
  (record_change), its author, its stamp and its operations (record_op), and this copy
  takes in and keeps exactly what that list does. A person's edit is a change of its
  own: a write-over of every value the copy holds in the field, in the order of `adds`,
  then the write. The copy takes the change in first, each operation by `todo.take`, an
  event with no data that reads the next operation of `taking`, and then sends it whole.
  A change a peer made reaches the copy as the same message and is taken in by the same
  events, so no copy can hold half of one.

  The registers are an observed-remove set of the standard `orset_*` algorithms, the
  operation-based form of it: a write is an add of the register's element with the
  write's dot as its tag, and a write-over removes the tag it names. A copy holds exactly
  the adds no write-over has removed, in `adds`, and keeps no tombstone: the layer that
  delivers the changes gives a copy each change once, whole, and only after every change
  its author had taken in when it made it, so a write-over always arrives after the
  write it names, and no write arrives twice. A write-over whose value is gone already
  changes nothing. The element is `id * 65536 + field`: a to-do is a uint32 and a field
  a uint16, so the pair is one uint64 below 2^48 and no two registers share one, whatever
  the numbers; it is below 2^53 as well, which the Interpreter's integers hold exactly,
  so no lane meets a limit another does not. What a set cannot carry is the value itself,
  a number and a text, so each live add has its value in `values`, beside it, kept by the
  standard `mv_value_*` algorithms. That is the whole of what this document adds to the
  merge.

  The clock is moved by what a copy sees as well as by what it does: a change made after
  reading someone else's sorts after it. It is moved once for each change taken in.

  Its peers. The copy sends to one route and names no peer of its own: `#people`, one
  group every copy sends to and reads. The route is bound to the delivery layer, which is
  not the list: the Mesh core's causal route (`delivery: causal`, SCE_MESH.md, docs/adr/
  0085 section 3.2) in the world. The layer tags each change, gives every copy each
  change exactly once and only once the copy holds every change it follows, repairs what
  a link lost, and forgets a change once every copy holds it. The list sees none of that:
  it takes in what it is given, in the order it is given it. What the copy's node is is
  the host's word (`todo.join`).

  A copy keeps every list in a room it is built with (`sce:limit`), and a write that
  would pass it fails half way, which no copy can undo. The host therefore gives a list
  less room than the build holds (`todo.room`), and a copy refuses a change of its own
  whole when it would give a register that holds no value one more value past the room:
  before it stamps or sends anything, counted in `full`. A change to a register that
  holds a value already writes over as many as it writes, and is never refused for the
  room. A change that is a person's own is the one judged, and what a person sent is
  taken in as it is, so the room is kept below the build's by what the people of one list
  can write at once.

  The host's word on what a member may do (`todo.role`) is judged on every copy: a change
  of this copy's own member that is not a writer's is refused, and a peer's change whose
  author is not a writer is taken in as no change; both are counted in `denied`.

  A send to the route the host gave no binding for is `error.execution` where it is
  made, which ends its block. So the copy takes a change in before it sends it, and the
  send is a block of its own: a copy with no router takes every change it makes in, and
  counts each send it could not make in `refusals`.

  The schedule is read from the values: `todo.agenda` asks what a to-do has scheduled in
  a window, and `todo.zone` gives the copy its host's time zones.

  `values` and `adds` are what a run compares across copies.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0" initial="open" datamodel="sce-static" name="todo_peer">
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_join.scxml" as="Join"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_edit.scxml" as="Edit"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_change.scxml" as="Change"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/shared/record_op.scxml" as="Op"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_agenda.scxml" as="Agenda"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_occurrence.scxml" as="Occurrence"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_timestamp.scxml" as="Hlc"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/orset_entry.scxml" as="Entry"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value.scxml" as="Value"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_send.scxml" as="HlcSend"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/hlc_receive.scxml" as="HlcReceive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_union.scxml" as="OrsetUnion"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/orset_live.scxml" as="OrsetLive"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_holds.scxml" as="MvValueHolds"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_keep.scxml" as="MvValueKeep"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/merge/mv_value_drop.scxml" as="MvValueDrop"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_schedule.scxml" as="Schedule"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_latest.scxml" as="EventLatest"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_conflict.scxml" as="EventConflict"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_agenda.scxml" as="EventAgenda"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_zone.scxml" as="Zone"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="sce:std/time/utc_from_local.scxml" as="UtcFromLocal"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_room.scxml" as="Room"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="todo_role.scxml" as="Role"/>
  <sce:import kind="event-schema" src="event_member.scxml" as="Member"/>
  <sce:import kind="algorithm" src="event_roster.scxml" as="EventRoster"/>
  <datamodel>
    <data id="node" sce:type="uint64" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="clock" sce:type="record:Hlc" sce:direction="out">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="stamp" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The change in hand: its stamp, which is the dot of every write in it, with its
         author as the dot's node. Every operation of one change is taken in before
         anything else reaches the copy, so the operations in `taking` are read with it. -->
    <data id="dot" sce:type="record:Hlc">
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <!-- The bounds of the lists a deployment may move are named (`sce:limit`): the
         lists of entries and of values are as large as the standard algorithms that
         return them, which carry the same names, so a build that gives a name a number
         moves the machine and the algorithms together. -->
    <data id="adds" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;[merge_entries=1024]" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="one" sce:type="list&lt;record:Entry&gt;[merge_entries=1024]"/>
    <data id="entry" sce:type="record:Entry">
      <sce:set name="element" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="values" sce:type="list&lt;record:Value&gt;[merge_values=512]" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The text a person types, held to the 32 bytes a person writes (todo_edit): a write
         has room for more (record_op), and a text past 32 that a person typed is refused
         as one past the room. -->
    <data id="typed" sce:type="string[32]" expr="''"/>
    <data id="held" sce:type="record:Value">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="wasLive" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="present" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="refusals" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="agenda" sce:type="list&lt;record:Occurrence&gt;[64]" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="local" sce:type="list&lt;record:Occurrence&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="occ" sce:type="record:Occurrence">
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="start" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="end" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nth" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="conflict" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="agendaNext" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <!-- The host's four time zones, a table of transitions each (todo.zone), and the
         table of the zone of the to-do the agenda is asked for. -->
    <data id="zoneStarts1" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets1" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts2" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets2" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts3" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets3" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts4" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets4" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneStarts" sce:type="list&lt;int64&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneOffsets" sce:type="list&lt;int32&gt;[64]"/>
    <data id="zoneRows" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="split" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="sched" sce:type="record:Schedule">
      <sce:set name="zone" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="start" expr="-1"/>
      <sce:set name="length" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="freq" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="interval" expr="1"/>
      <sce:set name="days" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="count" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="until" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="bymonth" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="mdPos" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="mdNeg" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="invalid" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="op6" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="on6" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="spPos" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="spNeg" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wkst" expr="1"/>
      <sce:set name="wnPos" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="wnNeg" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="yd5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn0" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn1" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn2" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn3" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn4" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="ydn5" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="gone" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="flag" expr="0"/>
    </data>
    <data id="rawCount" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="rawLast" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="utcSec" sce:type="int64" expr="0"/>
    <!-- How many values the host lets this copy hold (todo.room), 0 for no limit, and the
         changes a person made that were refused for it (`full`). What the change in hand
         is judged by: how many values it writes over (`gone`). -->
    <data id="roomValues" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="full" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="gone" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <!-- What the host lets each member do (todo.role), the changes that were refused for it
         (`denied`, a person's own and a peer's alike) and what the change in hand is judged
         by: whether its author may write. -->
    <data id="roster" sce:type="list&lt;record:Member&gt;[todo_roster=64]"/>
    <data id="denied" sce:type="uint32" expr="0" sce:direction="out"/>
    <data id="forbidden" sce:type="bool" expr="false"/>
    <data id="authorized" sce:type="bool" expr="true"/>
    <!-- The operations of the change in hand (`taking`), in the order of the change, the
         next to take in at `took`, each read by an event of its own that carries no data;
         and the operation in hand (`op`). A change of the copy's own is sent from
         `taking` whole once every operation of it is taken in. -->
    <data id="taking" sce:type="list&lt;record:Op&gt;[shared_parts=64]"/>
    <data id="took" sce:type="uint32" expr="0"/>
    <data id="op" sce:type="record:Op">
      <sce:set name="kind" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="id" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="field" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="value" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="text" expr="''"/>
      <sce:set name="wallTime" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="counter" expr="0"/>
      <sce:set name="nodeId" expr="0"/>
    </data>
  </datamodel>
  <state id="open">
    <transition event="todo.join" type="internal">
      <assign location="node" expr="_event.data.node"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- How many values the host lets this copy hold (todo.room). 0 is no limit. -->
    <transition event="todo.room" type="internal">
      <assign location="roomValues" expr="_event.data.values"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- What the host lets a member do (todo.role): the member takes the role, or is taken
         off the roster by a role of 0. A copy with no roster refuses no one. The roster is
         the host's word and the copies take it alike, as they take the room. -->
    <transition event="todo.role" type="internal">
      <assign location="roster" expr="EventRoster(roster, _event.data.node, _event.data.role)"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- A person's change of one field: judged whole, and taken in, or refused whole.

         The text is read first, into a place nothing else reads: a text past what a person
         writes is an assignment that fails and ends the block, so the change is refused
         whole, with the clock where it was and nothing sent. It is refused, and counted in
         `denied`, when the copy's member may not write (todo.role: with no roster set,
         anyone may; with one, a member whose role is a writer's); and, counted in `full`,
         when it would give a register that holds no value one more value past the room
         the host gave the copy (todo.room).

         A change that passes is stamped once and turned into its operations in `taking`:
         a write-over of each value the copy holds in the field, in the order of `adds`,
         each naming the dot of the value it writes over, then the write, whose dot is the
         change's stamp and is carried once (record_op). A change of more operations than
         `taking` holds is refused whole, by error.execution, before the clock moves. Then
         every operation is queued to be taken in here, and after them the change is queued
         to be sent: the copy holds the change before it sends it. -->
    <transition event="todo.edit" type="internal">
      <assign location="typed" expr="_event.data.text"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="_event.data.id"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + _event.data.field"/>
      <assign location="forbidden" expr="false"/>
      <if cond="len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="forbidden" expr="true"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === node &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="forbidden" expr="false"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="forbidden">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <assign location="gone" expr="0"/>
      <foreach array="adds" item="o">
        <if cond="o.element === entry.element">
          <assign location="gone" expr="gone + 1"/>
        </if>
      </foreach>
      <if cond="!forbidden &amp;&amp; roomValues &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; gone === 0 &amp;&amp; len(values) &gt;= roomValues">
        <assign location="full" expr="full + 1"/>
        <assign location="forbidden" expr="true"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="!forbidden">
        <assign location="stamp" expr="HlcSend(clock, _event.data.now, node)"/>
        <sce:clear target="taking"/>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <foreach array="adds" item="o">
          <if cond="o.element === entry.element">
            <assign location="op.kind" expr="1"/>
            <assign location="op.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
            <assign location="op.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
            <assign location="op.value" expr="0"/>
            <assign location="op.text" expr="''"/>
            <assign location="op.wallTime" expr="o.wallTime"/>
            <assign location="op.counter" expr="o.counter"/>
            <assign location="op.nodeId" expr="o.nodeId"/>
            <sce:append target="taking" expr="op"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
        <assign location="op.kind" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="op.id" expr="_event.data.id"/>
        <assign location="op.field" expr="_event.data.field"/>
        <assign location="op.value" expr="_event.data.value"/>
        <assign location="op.text" expr="_event.data.text"/>
        <assign location="op.wallTime" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="op.counter" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="op.nodeId" expr="0"/>
        <sce:append target="taking" expr="op"/>
        <assign location="clock" expr="stamp"/>
        <assign location="dot" expr="stamp"/>
        <foreach array="taking" item="t">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.take"/>
        </foreach>
        <send target="#_internal" event="todo.pass"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A peer's change, as the delivery layer gives it: once, whole, and after every
         change its author had taken in when it made it (docs/adr/0085, section 3). Its
         author is judged against the roster, on every copy: one the roster does not let
         write is taken in as no change, counted in `denied`. Otherwise every operation is
         queued to be taken in, in the order of the change, and then the clock is moved by
         the change's stamp, once: a peer's change by `hlc_receive`; a change of this copy's
         own node, which a copy that was started again from an older save is given back, up
         to its stamp, so that what the copy stamps next is after it and never with a dot it
         has used. The operations are read first: a change whose text does not fit what a
         copy keeps fails there, ends the block and is taken in not at all. -->
    <transition event="record_list.change" type="internal">
      <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
      <if cond="len(roster) &gt; 0">
        <assign location="authorized" expr="false"/>
        <foreach array="roster" item="m">
          <if cond="m.node === _event.data.by &amp;&amp; m.role &gt;= 2">
            <assign location="authorized" expr="true"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="!authorized">
        <assign location="denied" expr="denied + 1"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="authorized">
        <assign location="taking" expr="_event.data.ops"/>
        <assign location="took" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="dot.wallTime" expr="_event.data.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="dot.counter" expr="_event.data.counter"/>
        <assign location="dot.nodeId" expr="_event.data.by"/>
        <foreach array="taking" item="t">
          <send target="#_internal" event="todo.take"/>
        </foreach>
        <if cond="dot.nodeId === node &amp;&amp; (dot.wallTime &gt; clock.wallTime || (dot.wallTime === clock.wallTime &amp;&amp; dot.counter &gt; clock.counter))">
          <assign location="clock.wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
          <assign location="clock.counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
        </if>
        <if cond="dot.nodeId !== node">
          <assign location="clock" expr="HlcReceive(clock, dot, clock.wallTime, node)"/>
        </if>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The next operation of `taking`, taken in: a write gives its register one more
         value, once, and a write-over takes the value it names out. This is where every
         operation is merged, a copy's own and a peer's alike, and it keeps nothing of an
         operation but its effect.

         A write: its dot is the change's (`dot`). Unless its value is held already, its
         add is added and its value kept. The text is read into the value it is kept in. -->
    <transition event="todo.take" type="internal">
      <assign location="op" expr="taking[took]"/>
      <assign location="took" expr="took + 1"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="op.id"/>
      <assign location="entry.element" expr="entry.element * 65536 + op.field"/>
      <if cond="op.kind === 0">
        <assign location="held.text" expr="op.text"/>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="op.field"/>
        <assign location="held.value" expr="op.value"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="dot.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="dot.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="present" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <if cond="!present">
          <sce:clear target="one"/>
          <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
          <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetUnion(adds, one)"/>
          <assign location="values" expr="MvValueKeep(values, held)"/>
        </if>
      </if>
      <!-- A write-over: the add of the dot it names leaves `adds` and its value leaves
           `values`, and nothing is kept of it. Its write was given to this copy before it,
           so no later delivery brings the value back. A write-over whose value is gone
           already, because another change wrote it over first, changes nothing. -->
      <if cond="op.kind === 1">
        <assign location="entry.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="entry.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="entry.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="held.id" expr="op.id"/>
        <assign location="held.field" expr="op.field"/>
        <assign location="held.wallTime" expr="op.wallTime"/>
        <assign location="held.counter" expr="op.counter"/>
        <assign location="held.nodeId" expr="op.nodeId"/>
        <assign location="wasLive" expr="MvValueHolds(values, held)"/>
        <sce:clear target="one"/>
        <sce:append target="one" expr="entry"/>
        <assign location="adds" expr="OrsetLive(adds, one)"/>
        <assign location="values" expr="MvValueDrop(values, held)"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- A change of this copy's own, sent to its peers whole once every operation of it is
         taken in here: its author, its stamp and its operations, in their order. The send
         is the whole of the block, so one that fails where it is made fails alone. -->
    <transition event="todo.pass" type="internal">
      <send target="#people" event="record_list.change">
        <param name="by" expr="dot.nodeId"/>
        <param name="wallTime" expr="dot.wallTime"/>
        <param name="counter" expr="dot.counter"/>
        <param name="ops" expr="taking"/>
      </send>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host asks what a to-do has scheduled in a window: its occurrences there,
         read from the values the copy holds (event_agenda), for the host to show. Nothing
         is sent and nothing held changes; a to-do that has no schedule has no occurrences,
         and a window the scan cannot cover is a refusal that leaves the agenda empty. -->
    <transition event="todo.agenda" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="agenda"/>
      <assign location="agendaNext" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="rawCount" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="rawLast" expr="0"/>

      <!-- The schedule of the to-do: each field it holds, as the value written last
           (event_latest), and whether two people changed one at once (event_conflict).
           The numbers are event_agenda's. -->
      <assign location="sched.zone" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 15, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.start" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 16, -1)"/>
      <assign location="sched.length" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 17, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.freq" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 18, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.interval" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 19, 1)"/>
      <assign location="sched.days" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 20, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.count" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 21, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.until" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 22, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.bymonth" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 23, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.mdPos" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 24, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.mdNeg" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 25, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.invalid" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 26, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 45, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 46, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 47, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 48, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 49, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 50, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.op6" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 51, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 52, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 53, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 54, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 55, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 56, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 57, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.on6" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 58, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.spPos" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 28, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.spNeg" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 29, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.wkst" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 30, 1)"/>
      <assign location="sched.wnPos" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 31, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.wnNeg" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 32, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 33, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 34, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 35, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 36, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 37, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.yd5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 38, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn0" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 39, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn1" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 40, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn2" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 41, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn3" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 42, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn4" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 43, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.ydn5" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 44, 0)"/>
      <assign location="sched.gone" expr="EventLatest(values, _event.data.id, 9, 0)"/>
      <assign location="split" expr="EventConflict(values, _event.data.id)"/>
      <assign location="sched.flag" expr="0"/>
      <if cond="split">
        <assign location="sched.flag" expr="1"/>
      </if>

      <!-- That zone's table, as the one the conversion below reads. -->
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets"/>
      <assign location="zoneRows" expr="0"/>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 1">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts1" item="s1"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s1"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets1" item="o1"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o1"/></foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 2">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts2" item="s2"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s2"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets2" item="o2"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o2"/></foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 3">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts3" item="s3"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s3"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets3" item="o3"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o3"/></foreach>
      </if>
      <if cond="sched.zone === 4">
        <foreach array="zoneStarts4" item="s4"><sce:append target="zoneStarts" expr="s4"/><assign location="zoneRows" expr="zoneRows + 1"/></foreach>
        <foreach array="zoneOffsets4" item="o4"><sce:append target="zoneOffsets" expr="o4"/></foreach>
      </if>

      <!-- With no zone the wall-clock readings are UTC instants. -->
      <if cond="zoneRows === 0">
        <assign location="agenda" expr="EventAgenda(sched, values, _event.data.id, _event.data.windowStart, _event.data.windowEnd, _event.data.skip)"/>
        <foreach array="agenda" item="a">
          <assign location="rawCount" expr="rawCount + 1"/>
          <assign location="rawLast" expr="a.nth"/>
        </foreach>
      </if>
      <!-- With one, the schedule is read in the zone's wall clock over the window widened
           by a day each side, which holds every reading an offset can bring into the
           window, and each occurrence is turned back into an instant by the table
           (utc_from_local: the first of an overlap, a gap read with the offset before it)
           and kept when it overlaps the window as asked. Its end is its start and its
           length, which a change of the clock does not change. -->
      <if cond="zoneRows !== 0">
        <assign location="local" expr="EventAgenda(sched, values, _event.data.id, _event.data.windowStart - 86400000, _event.data.windowEnd + 86400000, _event.data.skip)"/>
        <foreach array="local" item="l">
          <assign location="rawCount" expr="rawCount + 1"/>
          <assign location="rawLast" expr="l.nth"/>
          <assign location="occ.id" expr="l.id"/>
          <assign location="occ.nth" expr="l.nth"/>
          <assign location="occ.conflict" expr="l.conflict"/>
          <assign location="utcSec" expr="UtcFromLocal(zoneStarts, zoneOffsets, l.start / 1000)"/>
          <assign location="occ.start" expr="utcSec * 1000 + l.start % 1000"/>
          <assign location="occ.end" expr="occ.start + (l.end - l.start)"/>
          <if cond="(occ.end &gt; _event.data.windowStart || occ.start &gt;= _event.data.windowStart) &amp;&amp; occ.start &lt; _event.data.windowEnd">
            <sce:append target="agenda" expr="occ"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </if>

      <!-- A page that is full says where the next begins. -->
      <if cond="rawCount === 64">
        <assign location="agendaNext" expr="rawLast + 1"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <!-- The host's time zones, one transition at a time (a message cannot carry a list),
         in order of start, after todo.zone_clear. They are the host's and not shared: each
         copy reads the zones its own host tells it. -->
    <transition event="todo.zone" type="internal">
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 1">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts1" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets1" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 2">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts2" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets2" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 3">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts3" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets3" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="_event.data.zone === 4">
        <sce:append target="zoneStarts4" expr="_event.data.start"/>
        <sce:append target="zoneOffsets4" expr="_event.data.offset"/>
      </if>
    </transition>

    <transition event="todo.zone_clear" type="internal">
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts1"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets1"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts2"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets2"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts3"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets3"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneStarts4"/>
      <sce:clear target="zoneOffsets4"/>
    </transition>

    <transition event="error.execution" type="internal">
      <assign location="refusals" expr="refusals + 1"/>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
